Findings:
  F-SG056-1  `router.execute` is NOT a pure `*args` passthrough. `estimated_cost` is a KEYWORD-ONLY parameter of
             `execute` (router.py:52) consumed by the pre-call budget check; it is NOT forwarded to the provider
             (`router.py:67` passes only `*args, **kwargs`). Consequence: through the reader the provider sees only
             `(image_bytes, prompt)`, so OpenCodeGoProvider's own per-job/monthly cap (opencode_go.py:242-253)
             always compares 0.0 — the router's `cost_budget` is the only binding cap. Packet's "pure passthrough"
             is imprecise; router untouched (out of ceiling); the fix is unaffected. Latent, worth the Architect's
             awareness.
